# The Windows column of the dashboard, v1: one Windows PC, Gemma 4 E2B, short-chat. Run by hand over SSH through
# scripts/windows_ssh_executor.py (windows/README.md), not by the night job. Same recipe rule as everywhere: a row's
# file= is what it measures, and each arm's file is its own (quant-per-arm-rule).
# runs=3: a new invocation purges the engine caches, so run 1 of a row writes them and is not admitted (firstEver).
#
# LiteRT-LM v0.19.0 built on the host. The NPU row is the repo's bundle for Intel Panther Lake, on the Intel dispatch.
windows litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm short-chat backend=cpu file=gemma-4-E2B-it.litertlm context-tokens=2048 runs=3
windows litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm short-chat backend=gpu file=gemma-4-E2B-it.litertlm context-tokens=2048 runs=3
windows litert-lm litert-community/gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm short-chat backend=npu file=gemma-4-E2B-it_intel_PTL.litertlm runs=3
# llama.cpp: the pinned release assets of windows/engine-pins.json. backend=gpu = the Vulkan asset, on the discrete GPU.
windows llama.cpp unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF short-chat file=gemma-4-E2B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf context-tokens=2048 runs=3
windows llama.cpp unsloth/gemma-4-E2B-it-GGUF short-chat backend=gpu file=gemma-4-E2B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf context-tokens=2048 runs=3
